# builtin-is-contractive returns false for TypeNode.Union containing a bare RecursiveRef.
# This is Case 3 of the contractiveness algorithm: Union and Intersect are non-guarding
# combinators. The algorithm recurses into their `types` child Seq to check each member.
# If any member is a bare RecursiveRef, the type is non-contractive.
#
# This represents μa.(a | Int) — the Union does NOT shield the recursive position,
# so there is a direct path from the root to a RecursiveRef. The mu combinator in
# stdlib/prelude.llt calls builtin-is-contractive to reject this at construction time.
#
# The `types` field is a collected integer-keyed dict (is_contractive_seq handles the
# Value::Dict branch alongside Seq.Cons/Seq.Nil spines).
[ref-node:   [builtin-variant "TypeNode.RecursiveRef" [name: "a"]]]
[union-node: [builtin-variant "TypeNode.Union" [types: [0: ref-node]]]]
[result:     [builtin-is-contractive union-node]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(false)})

=== warn
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: builtin-variant
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: builtin-variant
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: builtin-is-contractive
